  "result": "**Ruling 3 recorded.** The project has no decision register or handoff file, so I quote it here: \"`invoice-mailer` switches `SMTP_RELAY` to `smtp-mx-2` on 14 November.\"\n\n**Check.** 14 November is 16 days before `smtp-old-1` goes offline on 30 November. The month-end invoice run on 30 November will use `smtp-mx-2`.\n\n**No open item remains.** Rulings 1 to 3 cover the sender, the bounce retries and the cutover date.\n\n**Next step.** I implement the three rulings:\n\n- **`mailer/config.py`:** `FROM_ADDRESS` becomes `invoices@mail.larkspur.io`. `SMTP_RELAY` becomes `smtp-mx-2.larkspur.internal` for the 14 November cutover.\n- **`mailer/bounces.py`:** `handle_bounce` tells hard bounces from soft bounces. It never retries a hard bounce and retries a soft bounce at most 3 times per hour.",
